# The gateway is Linux; these files are executed there.
#
# eol=lf: guards against a Windows editor writing CRLF into a shebang line.
# A "#!/bin/bash\r" makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/bash\r". Not the cause of any past incident -- a precaution.
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.service     text eol=lf
miracle.cloud text eol=lf

# Binaries -- never let git guess or munge these.
*.db   binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
